1
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,929
<i>Previously on</i> Reacher...

2
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,515
No one can help me now.

3
00:00:10,641 --> 00:00:12,183
[Docherty] <i>This is Detective Tamara Green.</i>

4
00:00:12,184 --> 00:00:13,351
[Tamara] We got a call some other people

5
00:00:13,352 --> 00:00:14,978
<i>- want to ask you some questions.</i>
- [Reacher] <i>What is it the government's</i>

6
00:00:14,979 --> 00:00:16,396
so worried she might have given me?

7
00:00:16,397 --> 00:00:18,523
<i>- What are you looking for?</i>
- The flash drive.

8
00:00:18,524 --> 00:00:19,607
Who's your boss?

9
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:20,608
I'm Lila.

10
00:00:20,609 --> 00:00:22,777
She promised to do all she could
to find my father, and she did.

11
00:00:22,778 --> 00:00:24,195
Someone important.

12
00:00:24,196 --> 00:00:25,905
Congressman John Sampson.

13
00:00:25,906 --> 00:00:27,449
You're gonna blackmail him
with information

14
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:29,075
Anna stole for you from the Pentagon.

15
00:00:29,076 --> 00:00:30,952
<i>Jacob. How'd your nephew take the news?</i>

16
00:00:30,953 --> 00:00:31,995
I didn't track him down yet.

17
00:00:31,996 --> 00:00:33,413
Seems your sister may have
stolen some confidential data--

18
00:00:33,414 --> 00:00:34,748
Where are you going?

19
00:00:34,749 --> 00:00:36,208
[Jacob] <i>I want to find out all I can
about John Sampson.</i>

20
00:00:37,251 --> 00:00:38,334
[Reacher] <i>Okay.</i>

21
00:00:38,335 --> 00:00:39,711
- Let's go.
- You're coming?

22
00:00:39,712 --> 00:00:41,045
I'm good at not letting people

23
00:00:41,046 --> 00:00:42,297
<i>get away with things.</i>

24
00:00:42,298 --> 00:00:44,382
[grunting]

25
00:00:44,383 --> 00:00:47,010
[exciting music playing]

26
00:00:47,011 --> 00:00:47,969
[Foster] Take him.

27
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:49,638
[grunting]

28
00:01:01,692 --> 00:01:03,068
[pulsing music playing]

29
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:06,322
[Reacher grunting softly]

30
00:01:14,205 --> 00:01:15,330
Oh.

31
00:01:15,331 --> 00:01:16,457
Shoot.

32
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:26,842
Welcome to the party.

33
00:01:30,846 --> 00:01:32,514
How long was I out?

34
00:01:32,515 --> 00:01:34,016
No idea.

35
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,435
You were here when we woke up
a couple hours ago.

36
00:01:37,436 --> 00:01:40,563
They shot me with a tranquilizer dart.

37
00:01:40,564 --> 00:01:42,066
Twice.

38
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,317
How'd they get you?

39
00:01:44,318 --> 00:01:45,819
Hey.

40
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:47,237
Big Brother's watching.

41
00:01:47,238 --> 00:01:49,155
Probably listening, too.

42
00:01:49,156 --> 00:01:51,492
They already know how you got here.

43
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:54,495
No harm in telling me.

44
00:01:55,412 --> 00:01:57,790
I got home,
soon as I put my gun in my safe.

45
00:01:58,999 --> 00:02:01,209
Someone must have been
hiding in my house.

46
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:03,044
Smelled some chloroform.

47
00:02:03,045 --> 00:02:04,254
Here I am.

48
00:02:04,255 --> 00:02:05,880
I was walking to the bus stop
near my house

49
00:02:05,881 --> 00:02:07,549
to meet up with you in New York,

50
00:02:07,550 --> 00:02:09,676
felt a sting in my chest,

51
00:02:09,677 --> 00:02:11,970
looked down and there was a dart.

52
00:02:11,971 --> 00:02:14,264
Next thing I know, I'm looking at

53
00:02:14,265 --> 00:02:16,141
leaves on trees...

54
00:02:17,476 --> 00:02:18,811
Then I wake up here.

55
00:02:20,646 --> 00:02:22,188
I'm the only one who's tied down.

56
00:02:22,189 --> 00:02:24,358
Yeah. Have you seen yourself?

57
00:02:25,693 --> 00:02:27,110
Neither of us got a look at them.

58
00:02:27,111 --> 00:02:29,696
Have any idea who grabbed us?

59
00:02:29,697 --> 00:02:31,699
Maybe the guys
who took a run at you yesterday?

60
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:33,950
CIA.

61
00:02:33,951 --> 00:02:35,243
They told you that?

62
00:02:35,244 --> 00:02:37,412
Didn't need to.

63
00:02:37,413 --> 00:02:39,581
They didn't Mirandize us,
cite the Patriot Act

64
00:02:39,582 --> 00:02:41,666
or gin up any charges.

65
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:43,668
Means they don't have the power to arrest.

66
00:02:43,669 --> 00:02:45,920
But they had no problem
drugging, kidnapping

67
00:02:45,921 --> 00:02:47,964
and locking us up
in what I can only imagine

68
00:02:47,965 --> 00:02:51,217
is a basement, considering the smell
and lack of natural light.

69
00:02:51,218 --> 00:02:53,636
What federal agency
best fits that description?

70
00:02:53,637 --> 00:02:57,098
I thought the CIA wasn't supposed
to operate on U.S. soil.

71
00:02:57,099 --> 00:02:59,100
This shit's crazy.
'Cause abducting some drifter

72
00:02:59,101 --> 00:03:02,103
is one thing-- no offense--
but snatching up cops?

73
00:03:02,104 --> 00:03:03,439
So what does it all mean?

74
00:03:04,523 --> 00:03:06,608
- Means we're fucked.
- [door opens]

75
00:03:06,609 --> 00:03:08,611
[menacing music playing]

76
00:03:16,076 --> 00:03:18,078
[keypad beeping]

77
00:03:22,458 --> 00:03:25,335
- What's that?
- A stimulant. To clear your head.

78
00:03:25,336 --> 00:03:26,753
It's clear.

79
00:03:26,754 --> 00:03:28,254
I just do what they tell me.

80
00:03:28,255 --> 00:03:31,174
They tell you to get that needle
jammed in your eye?

81
00:03:31,175 --> 00:03:33,676
'Cause that's what's gonna happen,
you try and stick me with that.

82
00:03:33,677 --> 00:03:35,387
Sounds like he's plenty awake.

83
00:03:36,472 --> 00:03:37,973
Forget the shot, Doc.

84
00:03:40,392 --> 00:03:41,476
How's your neck?

85
00:03:41,477 --> 00:03:43,561
How's your head?

86
00:03:43,562 --> 00:03:45,773
Hear that tranq hangovers can be a bitch.

87
00:03:49,777 --> 00:03:51,361
Good luck trying to get those on me.

88
00:03:51,362 --> 00:03:52,987
Oh, they're going on.

89
00:03:52,988 --> 00:03:55,449
Question is are they going on
the easy way or the hard way?

90
00:03:59,536 --> 00:04:01,663
We upped the dose.

91
00:04:01,664 --> 00:04:03,623
So, you want to be a hard-ass

92
00:04:03,624 --> 00:04:06,084
or you want to get this over with,
Mr. Reacher?

93
00:04:06,085 --> 00:04:08,462
Just Reacher.

94
00:04:28,816 --> 00:04:30,317
[door closes]

95
00:04:38,993 --> 00:04:41,619
[Foster] Jack Reacher. No middle name.

96
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,580
Parents couldn't be bothered?

97
00:04:45,249 --> 00:04:48,167
What sort of given name is Jack?
Jack's a nickname.

98
00:04:48,168 --> 00:04:50,504
Why don't you tell me your names
and we can compare.

99
00:04:53,173 --> 00:04:54,298
Okay.

100
00:04:54,299 --> 00:04:55,591
You're Wynken,

101
00:04:55,592 --> 00:04:57,343
he's Blynken, that's Nod.

102
00:04:57,344 --> 00:04:59,262
From the Dutch lullaby.

103
00:04:59,263 --> 00:05:01,264
You call us that
because we put you to sleep?

104
00:05:01,265 --> 00:05:03,224
I call you that because,
before I leave this room,

105
00:05:03,225 --> 00:05:04,810
I'm gonna put all of you to sleep.

106
00:05:14,236 --> 00:05:17,030
Our techs combed through the data,
and the only thing that's on there

107
00:05:17,031 --> 00:05:20,992
is some student's mediocre sketches.

108
00:05:20,993 --> 00:05:22,368
Why?

109
00:05:22,369 --> 00:05:24,579
Maybe he doesn't apply himself.

110
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:25,747
Why do you have his jump drive?

111
00:05:25,748 --> 00:05:27,416
- I needed it.
- For what?

112
00:05:31,879 --> 00:05:34,172
See, I think you needed it
to make a copy of the drive you got

113
00:05:34,173 --> 00:05:36,842
from Anna Merrick
before she killed herself on the train.

114
00:05:38,052 --> 00:05:40,470
Where is that thumb drive?

115
00:05:40,471 --> 00:05:42,180
I have no idea what you're talking about.

116
00:05:42,181 --> 00:05:44,640
You're the only one
that came into contact with her,

117
00:05:44,641 --> 00:05:46,643
and the drive was not on her person.

118
00:05:47,811 --> 00:05:49,062
Do you think we're stupid?

119
00:05:49,063 --> 00:05:50,147
Yes.

120
00:05:53,025 --> 00:05:55,027
Who was the woman in the park?

121
00:05:56,111 --> 00:05:58,906
You know, the one that you let
open the drive and look at the contents?

122
00:06:01,658 --> 00:06:02,993
Where is she?

123
00:06:03,702 --> 00:06:05,411
Let me guess.

124
00:06:05,412 --> 00:06:07,413
You spent most of your resources on me
'cause you thought

125
00:06:07,414 --> 00:06:09,373
I'd be the problem and she'd be easy.

126
00:06:09,374 --> 00:06:12,835
Then, after I was drugged,
you went back for her but she was gone.

127
00:06:12,836 --> 00:06:14,963
Gave one of your junior officers the slip.

128
00:06:16,131 --> 00:06:18,257
You the one that was supposed
to be looking after her, Blynken?

129
00:06:18,258 --> 00:06:20,176
You look like the kind of jackass
who would get caught

130
00:06:20,177 --> 00:06:22,470
with his pants down and thumb up his ass.

131
00:06:22,471 --> 00:06:23,930
How about I put my foot up your ass?

132
00:06:23,931 --> 00:06:25,723
Try it.

133
00:06:25,724 --> 00:06:27,226
Not now.

134
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:30,186
Okay, we get it.

135
00:06:30,187 --> 00:06:32,021
You're a tough guy.

136
00:06:32,022 --> 00:06:33,689
We read your jacket.

137
00:06:33,690 --> 00:06:35,191
[pulsing music playing]

138
00:06:35,192 --> 00:06:36,776
But what about your friends out there?

139
00:06:36,777 --> 00:06:38,361
They're not my friends.

140
00:06:38,362 --> 00:06:39,862
I just met 'em today.

141
00:06:39,863 --> 00:06:42,115
You and Officer Merrick
were running around with the drive

142
00:06:42,116 --> 00:06:45,409
and we saw you conversing with
Detective Green before we detained you.

143
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:48,371
Now, we can only assume

144
00:06:48,372 --> 00:06:50,581
that they are coconspirators.

145
00:06:50,582 --> 00:06:52,500
We wanted to talk to you first
because we thought

146
00:06:52,501 --> 00:06:54,544
you might want to play ball
and spare them some pain,

147
00:06:54,545 --> 00:06:56,713
but apparently you don't give a shit
what happens to them.

148
00:07:02,678 --> 00:07:04,804
No one knows the three of you are here.

149
00:07:04,805 --> 00:07:07,265
We are treating you
like enemy combatants on U.S. soil.

150
00:07:07,266 --> 00:07:09,017
We can do whatever we want.

151
00:07:10,394 --> 00:07:12,311
Now, you...

152
00:07:12,312 --> 00:07:13,814
might be able to take it.

153
00:07:15,315 --> 00:07:16,817
For a while.

154
00:07:18,527 --> 00:07:20,612
But how do you think they'll hold up?

155
00:07:25,784 --> 00:07:27,451
Get him out of here.
Bring me the woman.

156
00:07:27,452 --> 00:07:28,954
Okay.

157
00:07:30,330 --> 00:07:32,206
Okay what?

158
00:07:32,207 --> 00:07:33,709
I'll answer your questions.

159
00:07:38,172 --> 00:07:39,673
That's better.

160
00:07:41,508 --> 00:07:43,468
So, why don't we try this again.

161
00:07:44,469 --> 00:07:47,556
Where is the drive that Anna Merrick
gave to you on the train?

162
00:07:49,349 --> 00:07:50,642
[grunting]

163
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,134
Told you.

164
00:08:37,231 --> 00:08:38,815
[intriguing music playing]

165
00:08:43,403 --> 00:08:46,822
It sounded like an all-out brawl
in there but now it's silent.

166
00:08:46,823 --> 00:08:48,450
Shit.

167
00:08:51,370 --> 00:08:53,080
[CIA officer] <i>Hello? Hello?</i>

168
00:08:56,124 --> 00:08:58,542
[Jacob] Holy shit.

169
00:08:58,543 --> 00:09:00,795
We thought they were kicking your ass.

170
00:09:00,796 --> 00:09:02,673
[Tamara] Where you going?

171
00:09:04,383 --> 00:09:05,884
Did he just leave us?

172
00:09:09,763 --> 00:09:11,265
[car alarm chirps]

173
00:09:22,734 --> 00:09:24,861
[phone ringing]

174
00:09:32,327 --> 00:09:34,161
- Hold that.
- All right.

175
00:09:34,162 --> 00:09:35,913
Phone means what I think it means?

176
00:09:35,914 --> 00:09:37,416
Company'll be here soon.

177
00:09:39,126 --> 00:09:40,627
[phone stops ringing]

178
00:09:41,837 --> 00:09:43,337
Maybe it's just a wrong number.

179
00:09:43,338 --> 00:09:45,048
[cell phones ringing]

180
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:48,175
They're calling cell phones now.
More than one.

181
00:09:48,176 --> 00:09:49,593
Means more than one guy's coming.

182
00:09:49,594 --> 00:09:52,388
- You get their guns?
- There were none. Must be locked up.

183
00:09:52,389 --> 00:09:54,307
They didn't think they needed
'em with you in cuffs.

184
00:09:54,308 --> 00:09:55,434
They were wrong.

185
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,395
Okay. Try that.

186
00:10:03,191 --> 00:10:04,734
Your wallets are on the table
in the other room.

187
00:10:04,735 --> 00:10:06,319
[Tamara] Got it.

188
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,696
[phones continue ringing]

189
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,452
Jesus.

190
00:10:25,172 --> 00:10:26,756
[grunts]

191
00:10:26,757 --> 00:10:28,300
They'll leave a message.

192
00:10:30,385 --> 00:10:31,969
- [grunting]
- We're running out of time!

193
00:10:31,970 --> 00:10:33,679
Just a little more.

194
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,182
You're gonna have to squeeze through.

195
00:10:37,559 --> 00:10:39,770
[grunts] I-I think I'm stuck.

196
00:10:46,902 --> 00:10:48,403
[Reacher] Go. Back down, back down.

197
00:10:57,829 --> 00:10:59,331
Close the door.

198
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:03,627
Go, go, go!

199
00:11:05,837 --> 00:11:07,297
[grunts]

200
00:11:19,226 --> 00:11:20,519
[wheels screeching in distance]

201
00:11:24,439 --> 00:11:25,773
There's more of 'em?

202
00:11:25,774 --> 00:11:27,526
To the alley.

203
00:11:45,961 --> 00:11:47,254
Get in!

204
00:11:48,755 --> 00:11:51,257
{\an8}I'm not CIA! My van has cats on it!

205
00:11:51,258 --> 00:11:52,426
[gunshots]

206
00:11:54,052 --> 00:11:55,220
Go!

207
00:11:59,599 --> 00:12:01,183
Who are you?

208
00:12:01,184 --> 00:12:03,811
Russell Plum. Freelance journalist.

209
00:12:03,812 --> 00:12:05,146
- [Jacob] Hey, look out!
- [van honks]

210
00:12:05,147 --> 00:12:06,480
[Russell] Oh, shit!

211
00:12:06,481 --> 00:12:08,190
[cars honking]

212
00:12:08,191 --> 00:12:11,110
I saw 'em bring you in on a gurney
yesterday, and you two

213
00:12:11,111 --> 00:12:13,404
were carried in a few hours later.
I've been watching that building

214
00:12:13,405 --> 00:12:14,822
- for weeks.
- Why?

215
00:12:14,823 --> 00:12:17,408
Figured it was a CIA black site,
and I was right.

216
00:12:17,409 --> 00:12:19,076
Saw you trying to escape, I came to help.

217
00:12:19,077 --> 00:12:20,578
What the hell for?

218
00:12:20,579 --> 00:12:23,497
For my story. We are gonna blow the lid
off what's going on in there.

219
00:12:23,498 --> 00:12:25,000
What's going on in there?

220
00:12:26,084 --> 00:12:28,377
- Answer the man.
- Me? I don't know.

221
00:12:28,378 --> 00:12:30,337
[Tamara] Well, what the fuck was your
sister involved in that I got snatched

222
00:12:30,338 --> 00:12:32,756
- by the goddamn CIA?
- I have no idea.

223
00:12:32,757 --> 00:12:35,426
Anna worked for the Pentagon,
so whatever's on the jump drives

224
00:12:35,427 --> 00:12:37,386
they're looking for
has to be military related.

225
00:12:37,387 --> 00:12:38,888
We need to know for sure.

226
00:12:38,889 --> 00:12:40,055
How are we gonna find out?

227
00:12:40,056 --> 00:12:43,434
I have someone who can help.
Just got to get down to DC.

228
00:12:43,435 --> 00:12:47,271
Down to D.C.?
Look out your window, man.

229
00:12:47,272 --> 00:12:48,857
We are in D.C.

230
00:12:49,858 --> 00:12:51,442
[uneasy music playing]

231
00:12:51,443 --> 00:12:53,403
What is going on?

232
00:13:01,661 --> 00:13:03,163
[tires screeching]

233
00:13:19,137 --> 00:13:22,306
I'm investigating
the world's most secretive agency.

234
00:13:22,307 --> 00:13:23,808
I use precaution.

235
00:13:31,483 --> 00:13:33,151
- [keys jingling]
- [lock clicks]

236
00:13:44,996 --> 00:13:46,706
Pen is mightier than the sword.

237
00:13:47,916 --> 00:13:49,458
Depends on who's wielding the sword.

238
00:13:49,459 --> 00:13:51,961
[Russell] All I need is a pen. You'll see.

239
00:13:51,962 --> 00:13:53,837
- [Tamara] What is all this?
- [Russell] My research.

240
00:13:53,838 --> 00:13:55,465
Been investigating the CIA for years.

241
00:13:56,341 --> 00:13:58,008
- Because?
- Because they're involved

242
00:13:58,009 --> 00:14:00,469
in all kinds of shady shit that
the public needs to know about.

243
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:03,347
They trained Manson, covered up Kennedy,

244
00:14:03,348 --> 00:14:05,349
got me fired from <i>The Washington Post.</i>

245
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:07,059
Now I just have to prove all of it.

246
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,227
You wrote for the <i>Post?</i>

247
00:14:08,228 --> 00:14:11,313
<i>Post.</i> Then the <i>Examiner.</i>
Then the <i>Washington City Paper.</i>

248
00:14:11,314 --> 00:14:13,274
Then a few free periodicals.

249
00:14:13,275 --> 00:14:14,650
None of 'em wanted the truth.

250
00:14:14,651 --> 00:14:17,152
They're all beholden to their
corporate and political overlords.

251
00:14:17,153 --> 00:14:20,114
Now I'm strictly Internet-based.

252
00:14:20,115 --> 00:14:23,117
I give it directly to the people.

253
00:14:23,118 --> 00:14:24,619
No filters.

254
00:14:26,621 --> 00:14:28,163
[Jacob] Holy shit.

255
00:14:28,164 --> 00:14:31,041
Hey, we're across the street
from the CIA building.

256
00:14:31,042 --> 00:14:33,711
Stay away from the windows.

257
00:14:33,712 --> 00:14:34,878
Are we safe here?

258
00:14:34,879 --> 00:14:36,880
Probably.

259
00:14:36,881 --> 00:14:38,549
They know we got away in a vehicle.

260
00:14:38,550 --> 00:14:40,593
It's unlikely they'd look for us
on their own block.

261
00:14:40,594 --> 00:14:42,720
Yeah, I circled around the back
and came in through the rear entrance.

262
00:14:42,721 --> 00:14:45,348
Nobody knows we're here.
Hey, you want to watch 'em?

263
00:14:46,349 --> 00:14:48,892
I hid cameras all over the roof.

264
00:14:48,893 --> 00:14:50,604
Check this out.

265
00:14:52,564 --> 00:14:53,940
That's you.

266
00:14:54,691 --> 00:14:57,610
Most people who work for the CIA
don't know where the black sites are.

267
00:14:57,611 --> 00:14:58,736
How do you know?

268
00:14:58,737 --> 00:15:01,447
Well, I traced payments
for construction work

269
00:15:01,448 --> 00:15:03,699
done on one of the exposed
overseas black sites

270
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:05,326
through a maze of shell companies.

271
00:15:05,327 --> 00:15:08,037
Now, one of those shells

272
00:15:08,038 --> 00:15:10,623
was connected to an LLC
that has no visible income

273
00:15:10,624 --> 00:15:12,750
but somehow was able to purchase
that building across the street.

274
00:15:12,751 --> 00:15:15,085
- So...
- [tapping monitor]

275
00:15:15,086 --> 00:15:16,920
I looked at a map...

276
00:15:16,921 --> 00:15:18,464
and check this out.

277
00:15:18,465 --> 00:15:21,842
It's over one of the old steam tunnels
that runs under Embassy Row.

278
00:15:21,843 --> 00:15:25,137
There has to be an illegal
CIA spy op, right?

279
00:15:25,138 --> 00:15:28,682
So, got a sweet off-the-books deal
for this loft

280
00:15:28,683 --> 00:15:30,851
because the building is...

281
00:15:30,852 --> 00:15:32,603
well, it's technically condemned.

282
00:15:32,604 --> 00:15:35,022
Landlord's fighting it in court
but he's desperate for cash flow.

283
00:15:35,023 --> 00:15:36,482
Set up shop and I started watching.

284
00:15:36,483 --> 00:15:38,609
And then I see 'em

285
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:41,528
bringing in steel plating
and welding equipment.

286
00:15:41,529 --> 00:15:44,740
I assume it was for cages.

287
00:15:44,741 --> 00:15:46,909
Right? Did they lock you guys in cages?

288
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:49,370
Yeah. For a while.

289
00:15:49,371 --> 00:15:50,913
I knew it.

290
00:15:50,914 --> 00:15:53,123
I'm gonna blow the lid off this thing.

291
00:15:53,124 --> 00:15:54,917
I'm gonna win my Pulitzer.

292
00:15:54,918 --> 00:15:57,169
I'm gonna need your testimony.

293
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:58,420
No.

294
00:15:58,421 --> 00:16:01,465
But... I rescued you.

295
00:16:01,466 --> 00:16:03,759
You need to forget you ever met us.

296
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,929
You've stumbled into something
way bigger than you can handle.

297
00:16:07,472 --> 00:16:08,847
- My story i--
- [Tamara] People already

298
00:16:08,848 --> 00:16:10,850
died over this, Russell.
You don't want to be next.

299
00:16:12,435 --> 00:16:14,229
Okay. What do we do now?

300
00:16:15,105 --> 00:16:16,522
We?

301
00:16:16,523 --> 00:16:19,066
I thought you were just gonna ride it out
till you get your pension.

302
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:22,319
I was drugged and taken
150 miles from my home.

303
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,696
I'm in this shit now.

304
00:16:23,697 --> 00:16:26,365
Public transportation's risky
with the CIA looking for us.

305
00:16:26,366 --> 00:16:28,784
My sister was on the train in Philly.

306
00:16:28,785 --> 00:16:30,619
So her car's still
got to be in her garage.

307
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,870
She lived near here.

308
00:16:31,871 --> 00:16:33,997
They've probably
ransacked the place already.

309
00:16:33,998 --> 00:16:36,667
Odds are it's safe to go.
Keep your heads on a swivel.

310
00:16:36,668 --> 00:16:37,751
[Tamara] What are you gonna do?

311
00:16:37,752 --> 00:16:39,002
Go look for John Sampson.

312
00:16:39,003 --> 00:16:41,964
The congressman? What the hell
does he have to do with this?

313
00:16:41,965 --> 00:16:43,465
That's what I'm gonna find out.

314
00:16:43,466 --> 00:16:44,842
- These burners?
- [Russell] Yeah.

315
00:16:44,843 --> 00:16:46,094
Help yourself.

316
00:16:47,345 --> 00:16:48,721
I've already memorized your numbers.

317
00:16:48,722 --> 00:16:50,180
I'll text you mine.

318
00:16:50,181 --> 00:16:51,223
Call me after you get the car.

319
00:16:51,224 --> 00:16:52,475
What do you want me to do?

320
00:16:55,729 --> 00:16:57,605
Start looking for a new place to live.

321
00:17:00,483 --> 00:17:01,985
Man.

322
00:17:03,486 --> 00:17:05,488
[foreboding music playing]

323
00:17:20,587 --> 00:17:23,423
- [metal detector warbling]
[guard] Step forward.

324
00:17:42,859 --> 00:17:44,568
Is Representative Sampson in today?

325
00:17:44,569 --> 00:17:46,195
Yes, he is. And you are?

326
00:17:46,196 --> 00:17:47,738
A constituent.

327
00:17:47,739 --> 00:17:50,407
I'm sorry, sir. His schedule is full.

328
00:17:50,408 --> 00:17:52,034
May I take your name?

329
00:17:52,035 --> 00:17:53,660
How about I just write him a note?

330
00:17:53,661 --> 00:17:55,163
Of course.

331
00:18:09,928 --> 00:18:12,388
Tell him I'll be at the food trucks
by the National Mall.

332
00:18:39,332 --> 00:18:41,042
[Tamara] Someone was
looking for the drive.

333
00:18:49,259 --> 00:18:51,094
Your nephew?

334
00:18:54,055 --> 00:18:56,098
Yeah, wish he'd call me back.

335
00:18:56,099 --> 00:18:57,600
Starting to worry.

336
00:19:00,103 --> 00:19:02,646
You know college kids.

337
00:19:02,647 --> 00:19:05,149
I'd go days before calling my mom back.

338
00:19:10,488 --> 00:19:12,574
There's the garage. I'll get the keys.

339
00:19:21,082 --> 00:19:22,666
Hey, they're not here.

340
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:23,917
[door opens]

341
00:19:23,918 --> 00:19:25,420
Forget the keys.

342
00:19:27,630 --> 00:19:28,839
Where's the car?

343
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,424
I don't know.

344
00:19:30,425 --> 00:19:32,427
[door closes]

345
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:37,139
Anna's Pentagon employee badge is here.

346
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:40,183
Under some mail. Old mail.

347
00:19:40,184 --> 00:19:42,061
Like she hasn't used it in a few weeks.

348
00:19:43,146 --> 00:19:45,272
Your sister must have left in a hurry.

349
00:19:45,273 --> 00:19:46,649
Didn't even finish her meal.

350
00:19:50,486 --> 00:19:52,988
Fuck.

351
00:19:52,989 --> 00:19:54,365
Still warm.

352
00:19:58,077 --> 00:20:00,079
[grunting]

353
00:20:25,104 --> 00:20:26,105
[shouts]

354
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,733
[groans]

355
00:20:31,277 --> 00:20:32,444
Thank you.

356
00:20:32,445 --> 00:20:34,113
Just returning the favor.

357
00:20:53,091 --> 00:20:56,093
Major Reacher. Don't get up.

358
00:20:56,094 --> 00:20:58,720
I'm Elspeth Sampson,
the congressman's wife.

359
00:20:58,721 --> 00:21:01,056
This is our head of security, Springfield.

360
00:21:01,057 --> 00:21:03,308
Smart move,
leaving your full name and rank

361
00:21:03,309 --> 00:21:05,727
so we could look you up,
know who we're dealing with.

362
00:21:05,728 --> 00:21:07,271
Otherwise we might not have come.

363
00:21:08,523 --> 00:21:10,440
[Elspeth] You said you were
one of John's constituents,

364
00:21:10,441 --> 00:21:12,526
but records don't show
a North Carolina address.

365
00:21:12,527 --> 00:21:14,069
Or any address.

366
00:21:14,070 --> 00:21:16,989
Don't have one. I served
in North Carolina three times, though,

367
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:18,408
so I figured that was close enough.

368
00:21:19,492 --> 00:21:21,535
I see.

369
00:21:21,536 --> 00:21:23,245
And why did you choose to meet here?

370
00:21:23,246 --> 00:21:24,997
Hadn't eaten since yesterday.

371
00:21:24,998 --> 00:21:26,081
Why not?

372
00:21:26,082 --> 00:21:28,543
'Cause I was drugged
and abducted by the CIA.

373
00:21:30,003 --> 00:21:31,504
Then you should finish your meal.

374
00:21:37,427 --> 00:21:40,429
Most scandals involve something
the wife doesn't know about.

375
00:21:40,430 --> 00:21:42,014
Sending you was a statement.

376
00:21:42,015 --> 00:21:44,558
John didn't send me.

377
00:21:44,559 --> 00:21:46,977
I wanted to see for myself
if you were worth his time

378
00:21:46,978 --> 00:21:49,521
or if this is just
some pathetic attempt at blackmail.

379
00:21:49,522 --> 00:21:52,816
I don't want anything
from your husband except the truth.

380
00:21:52,817 --> 00:21:55,610
A Pentagon clerk killed herself
in front of me, night before last.

381
00:21:55,611 --> 00:21:58,322
With John's name on her lips?

382
00:21:59,407 --> 00:22:01,576
- Basically.
- "Basically" doesn't cut it.

383
00:22:02,744 --> 00:22:05,120
Why do you think my husband
has anything to do with this?

384
00:22:05,121 --> 00:22:07,039
With respect, my questions concern matters

385
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,707
your husband probably
wouldn't share with you,

386
00:22:08,708 --> 00:22:10,709
so even if I asked,
it's unlikely you'd know the answer.

387
00:22:10,710 --> 00:22:12,295
John and I have no secrets.

388
00:22:13,379 --> 00:22:14,756
Maybe.

389
00:22:21,095 --> 00:22:24,222
Hotel, few blocks from here.

390
00:22:24,223 --> 00:22:26,058
Congressman's speaking
at a dinner there tonight.

391
00:22:26,059 --> 00:22:27,559
He's in his suite now, preparing.

392
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:29,895
He'll be expecting you.

393
00:22:29,896 --> 00:22:32,607
You get five minutes of his time,
not one second more.

394
00:22:37,403 --> 00:22:38,905
Can you give me a ride?

395
00:22:40,406 --> 00:22:41,990
I could.

396
00:22:41,991 --> 00:22:43,992
[vehicle doors close]

397
00:22:43,993 --> 00:22:45,495
[engine starts]

398
00:22:46,913 --> 00:22:48,915
[vehicle departs]

399
00:22:50,291 --> 00:22:52,834
[grunts]

400
00:22:52,835 --> 00:22:54,587
Yeah, that should hold him.

401
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:58,548
I'll hold on to his Glock.

402
00:22:58,549 --> 00:23:00,050
You could use a weapon.

403
00:23:00,051 --> 00:23:02,011
Your sister keep any guns in the house?

404
00:23:04,430 --> 00:23:06,307
There's... the one.

405
00:23:07,934 --> 00:23:09,851
But she...

406
00:23:09,852 --> 00:23:12,687
Right. Sorry.

407
00:23:12,688 --> 00:23:14,690
[phone rings]

408
00:23:16,109 --> 00:23:18,778
If that was the CIA,
they'd be calling this guy's cell.

409
00:23:21,656 --> 00:23:23,658
Answer it. Pretend you're Anna.

410
00:23:25,034 --> 00:23:26,536
[ringing continues]

411
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:34,001
Hello.

412
00:23:35,837 --> 00:23:37,587
This is she.

413
00:23:37,588 --> 00:23:38,798
No, he isn't.

414
00:23:40,007 --> 00:23:42,677
I have no idea.
But if I hear from him, I'll tell him.

415
00:23:44,679 --> 00:23:47,597
I really have to go.
I'm in the middle of something.

416
00:23:47,598 --> 00:23:49,100
Thank you for calling.

417
00:23:53,563 --> 00:23:55,773
That was one of Ben's football coaches.

418
00:23:57,817 --> 00:23:59,193
He never showed for practice.

419
00:24:08,161 --> 00:24:10,163
- [indistinct chatter]
- [piano playing gently]

420
00:24:15,459 --> 00:24:17,461
[elevator bell dings]

421
00:24:27,138 --> 00:24:28,472
<i>[knocking]</i>

422
00:24:31,517 --> 00:24:32,726
Snap.

423
00:24:32,727 --> 00:24:34,812
Come in, Reacher. We need to talk.

424
00:24:36,230 --> 00:24:39,107
Crackle. Pop.

425
00:24:39,108 --> 00:24:40,692
[Snap] Have a seat.

426
00:24:40,693 --> 00:24:43,154
No, thanks. Where's Sampson?

427
00:24:44,530 --> 00:24:45,739
You're in big trouble.

428
00:24:45,740 --> 00:24:48,200
You told us Anna Merrick didn't
say anything to you on the subway

429
00:24:48,201 --> 00:24:49,743
- the other night.
- She didn't.

430
00:24:49,744 --> 00:24:52,996
Well, that's not what you wrote in the
note that you sent to the congressman.

431
00:24:52,997 --> 00:24:55,207
You lied to federal investigators.

432
00:24:55,208 --> 00:24:56,708
People go to prison for that.

433
00:24:56,709 --> 00:24:58,585
- Not me.
- [Snap] Why not?

434
00:24:58,586 --> 00:25:01,671
You didn't identify yourselves.
You could've been anybody.

435
00:25:01,672 --> 00:25:04,424
So, if we showed you some ID
you would have told us the truth?

436
00:25:04,425 --> 00:25:05,675
Sure.

437
00:25:05,676 --> 00:25:08,763
So... did she say John Sampson's name?

438
00:25:10,097 --> 00:25:11,097
No.

439
00:25:11,098 --> 00:25:12,807
Then where did you hear it?

440
00:25:12,808 --> 00:25:14,392
From the CIA.

441
00:25:14,393 --> 00:25:15,894
When did you talk to the CIA?

442
00:25:15,895 --> 00:25:17,146
When they kidnapped me.

443
00:25:21,484 --> 00:25:23,193
Why would the CIA kidnap you?

444
00:25:23,194 --> 00:25:24,694
They think I know something.

445
00:25:24,695 --> 00:25:25,779
Do you?

446
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,656
I know they're running
an illegal black site

447
00:25:27,657 --> 00:25:29,950
out of an old building
on the corner of Hopkins and P.

448
00:25:29,951 --> 00:25:31,660
Go see for yourselves.

449
00:25:31,661 --> 00:25:35,163
The way I see it, the CIA
knows way more about this than I do.

450
00:25:35,164 --> 00:25:36,706
If you have questions, ask them.

451
00:25:36,707 --> 00:25:38,041
You want some advice?

452
00:25:38,042 --> 00:25:39,125
No.

453
00:25:39,126 --> 00:25:41,503
You were in the wrong place
at the wrong time

454
00:25:41,504 --> 00:25:42,963
and you saw the wrong thing.

455
00:25:42,964 --> 00:25:45,006
Something fucked-up
happened in front of you

456
00:25:45,007 --> 00:25:47,008
and, as a former investigator,
you want to look into it

457
00:25:47,009 --> 00:25:49,594
'cause your instincts
say that things don't smell right.

458
00:25:49,595 --> 00:25:53,640
But this is not a case you're gonna close.

459
00:25:53,641 --> 00:25:55,308
Walk away.

460
00:25:55,309 --> 00:25:57,852
'Cause if you keep sticking your nose
where it doesn't belong,

461
00:25:57,853 --> 00:25:59,521
you're gonna get it cut off.

462
00:25:59,522 --> 00:26:01,524
[tense music playing]

463
00:26:12,493 --> 00:26:14,244
- [Tamara] <i>Yeah.</i>
- Have any trouble?

464
00:26:14,245 --> 00:26:16,496
Nothing we couldn't handle.
What about you?

465
00:26:16,497 --> 00:26:18,707
Same. Need you to pick me up.

466
00:26:18,708 --> 00:26:21,293
Can't. Anna's car isn't here.

467
00:26:21,294 --> 00:26:22,920
Had Docherty put out a BOLO.

468
00:26:24,046 --> 00:26:26,131
<i>Federal agents could have
taken the car to search it.</i>

469
00:26:26,132 --> 00:26:27,716
Maybe.

470
00:26:27,717 --> 00:26:29,050
<i>But they tossed the house.</i>

471
00:26:29,051 --> 00:26:30,719
<i>Probably could have searched
the car in the garage at the same time.</i>

472
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:32,137
Maybe it was stolen.

473
00:26:32,138 --> 00:26:33,513
That'd be quite a coincidence.

474
00:26:33,514 --> 00:26:34,973
<i>Coincidences are rare.</i>

475
00:26:34,974 --> 00:26:38,643
So what we're left with
is Anna drove her car to Philly.

476
00:26:38,644 --> 00:26:40,645
Then, for some reason,

477
00:26:40,646 --> 00:26:43,023
got out and got on the subway.

478
00:26:43,024 --> 00:26:45,442
- Why would she do that?
<i>- No idea.</i>

479
00:26:45,443 --> 00:26:47,110
Anything else?

480
00:26:47,111 --> 00:26:49,070
Ben missed football practice.

481
00:26:49,071 --> 00:26:50,739
<i>He's on scholarship.</i>

482
00:26:50,740 --> 00:26:52,532
<i>Knows if he screws up, he'll lose it.</i>

483
00:26:52,533 --> 00:26:54,909
<i>I don't care what
that woman he met looks like,</i>

484
00:26:54,910 --> 00:26:58,038
<i>he's not risking his full ride
for any girl.</i>

485
00:26:58,039 --> 00:27:00,624
We've got to get back to Philly
and find him.

486
00:27:01,709 --> 00:27:03,043
Public transpo's out.

487
00:27:03,044 --> 00:27:04,252
<i>We need a car.</i>

488
00:27:04,253 --> 00:27:06,547
I know someone
who has a car we can borrow.

489
00:27:08,632 --> 00:27:09,632
You're back.

490
00:27:09,633 --> 00:27:10,884
Anybody see you come in?

491
00:27:10,885 --> 00:27:12,510
- I came in the back.
- Good.

492
00:27:12,511 --> 00:27:15,180
'Cause two guys in suits
driving a sedan with government plates

493
00:27:15,181 --> 00:27:16,848
just pulled into the black site.

494
00:27:16,849 --> 00:27:20,226
Wouldn't be CIA with those plates,
but I don't know.

495
00:27:20,227 --> 00:27:23,396
Could be FBI or NSA, but they like to use
generic state plates, not draw attention,

496
00:27:23,397 --> 00:27:26,524
so my guess is that they're DCSA,
maybe DCIS.

497
00:27:26,525 --> 00:27:29,152
Anyway, they kicked in the door,
they went inside.

498
00:27:29,153 --> 00:27:31,363
They're not gonna find anything,
because the CIA bugged out

499
00:27:31,364 --> 00:27:33,782
just before they got there.
There goes my story.

500
00:27:33,783 --> 00:27:35,825
Place is completely cleared out now.

501
00:27:35,826 --> 00:27:37,911
Wonder how they found out
about the black site.

502
00:27:37,912 --> 00:27:39,829
- I told 'em.
- Why would you do that?

503
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:42,499
'Cause I want to give the CIA
something to worry about besides us.

504
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:44,542
- Us?
- I need your help.

505
00:27:44,543 --> 00:27:46,294
I knew you'd come around.

506
00:27:46,295 --> 00:27:48,088
Okay, but before we go,
I need a new burner.

507
00:27:48,089 --> 00:27:50,799
For all I know, they grabbed the signal
off mine during my meeting with the feds.

508
00:27:50,800 --> 00:27:53,468
- Could be trying to track it right now.
- Let me just get my shit.

509
00:27:53,469 --> 00:27:56,179
And don't worry. I'm a valuable asset.
You'll see.

510
00:27:56,180 --> 00:27:57,806
I can dig up any information you need.

511
00:27:57,807 --> 00:28:00,016
You will not be sorry.

512
00:28:00,017 --> 00:28:02,560
I'm gonna need your full background
for my article.

513
00:28:02,561 --> 00:28:05,397
I mean, I can tell you're former military
by the way you carry yourself.

514
00:28:05,398 --> 00:28:07,690
And your pointed questions
and limited answers,

515
00:28:07,691 --> 00:28:11,528
well, makes me think
you're some kind of investigator.

